tags: device-place, location

A fact of a device: where the device is, as a text for a person. For example the room,
the rack or the slot.

The value is UTF-8 text, one line, 256 bytes or less. Example: rack 3, slot 2. A
program does not read a meaning from it.

An absent fact: the node gives no place. The node is bound: it attests the fact.

